        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'End of an era': EU flag outside parliament signals shift in Hungary Issued on: 09/05/2026 - 18:10 Modified: 09/05/2026 - 18:15 Hungary may be entering a new political phase as the European Union flag appeared alongside the national flag outside parliament, symbolising a potential shift in the country’s long-standing confrontation with Brussels. FRANCE 24 International Affairs Editor Shirley Sippon said the change comes after years in which Viktor Orban positioned Hungary as a key challenger within the EU, particularly on issues ranging from veto power to Ukraine policy and rule-of-law disputes. Contact tracing begins after Hantavirus-hit cruise passengers disembarks in St. Helena 09/05/2026 Europe Moscow marks Victory Day amid tight security 09/05/2026 Europe 'Atmosphere closer to wartime': Moscow’s muted Victory Day reflects growing security fears 09/05/2026 Europe 'Clean break' with Orban: Hungary's Magyar to usher in 'new era' 09/05/2026 Europe Magyar to succeed Orban as Hungary's new prime minister 09/05/2026 Europe Jordan sees collapse in tourism since Iran war 09/05/2026 Middle East Hungary’s Magyar set to be sworn in as new prime minister 09/05/2026 Europe US awaits Iran's response to latest proposal amid technical ceasefire 09/05/2026 Middle East Pentagon releases new files on UFOs 09/05/2026 Americas"
